{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The protected observation `y` is a top-level data variable and is observed exactly once with the built-in sampling statement `y ~ normal(y_hat, sigma_y);`. It is not referenced before observation or in transformed blocks. All parameters have exactly one built-in prior sampling statement before their use in the model block.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> N;
  int<lower=0> n_pair;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=n_pair> pair;
  vector[N] treatment;
  vector[N] y;
}
parameters {
  vector[n_pair] a;
  real beta;
  real mu_a;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_a;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_y;
}
transformed parameters {
  vector[N] y_hat;

  for (i in 1 : N) {
    y_hat[i] = a[pair[i]] + beta * treatment[i];
  }
}
model {
  mu_a ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma_a ~ uniform(0, 100);
  sigma_y ~ uniform(0, 100);

  a ~ normal(100 * mu_a, sigma_a);
  beta ~ normal(0, 1);
  y ~ normal(y_hat, sigma_y);
}
